; A counter machine adds counter c into counter d: while c is not zero,
; decrement c and increment d.  A counter's value is its number of rows; the
; zero test is an absence.  One outcome under the one-match step.  Under every,
; the three copies of (c) are three matches that all need the one (at loop):
; none can be told apart, so every has no step (a sequential machine is not a
; synchronous one).
(step one)
(at loop)
(c) (c) (c)
(d)
(rule decrement (take (at loop) (c)) (make (at add)))
(rule finished (take (at loop)) (absent (c)) (make (halt)))
(rule increment (take (at add)) (make (d) (at loop)))
